EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
   EExxaammppllee 11: Creating a RAID-Z Storage Pool
     The following command creates a pool with a single raidz root vdev that
     consists of six disks:
           # zzppooooll ccrreeaattee _t_a_n_k rraaiiddzz _s_d_a _s_d_b _s_d_c _s_d_d _s_d_e _s_d_f

   EExxaammppllee 22: Creating a Mirrored Storage Pool
     The following command creates a pool with two mirrors, where each mirror
     contains two disks:
           # zzppooooll ccrreeaattee _t_a_n_k mmiirrrroorr _s_d_a _s_d_b mmiirrrroorr _s_d_c _s_d_d

   EExxaammppllee 33: Creating a ZFS Storage Pool by Using Partitions
     The following command creates a non-redundant pool using two disk parti‐
     tions:
           # zzppooooll ccrreeaattee _t_a_n_k _s_d_a_1 _s_d_b_2

   EExxaammppllee 44: Creating a ZFS Storage Pool by Using Files
     The following command creates a non-redundant pool using files.  While
     not recommended, a pool based on files can be useful for experimental
     purposes.
           # zzppooooll ccrreeaattee _t_a_n_k _/_p_a_t_h_/_t_o_/_f_i_l_e_/_a _/_p_a_t_h_/_t_o_/_f_i_l_e_/_b

   EExxaammppllee 55: Managing Hot Spares
     The following command creates a new pool with an available hot spare:
           # zzppooooll ccrreeaattee _t_a_n_k mmiirrrroorr _s_d_a _s_d_b ssppaarree _s_d_c

   EExxaammppllee 66: Creating a ZFS Pool with Mirrored Separate Intent Logs
     The following command creates a ZFS storage pool consisting of two, two-
     way mirrors and mirrored log devices:
           # zzppooooll ccrreeaattee _p_o_o_l mmiirrrroorr _s_d_a _s_d_b mmiirrrroorr _s_d_c _s_d_d lloogg mmiirrrroorr _s_d_e
           _s_d_f

